# {{.Name}}

An HTTP service built on [mizu](https://github.com/go-mizu/mizu).

## Running it

```
go mod tidy
go run .
```

It listens on `:8080`, or on `$ADDR` when that is set.

```
curl localhost:8080/
curl localhost:8080/hello/ada
curl localhost:8080/livez
```

## Testing it

```
go test ./...
```

The tests serve the real application through an in-memory recorder, so they
open no sockets and pick no ports. That is what makes them fast enough to run
on every save and safe to run in parallel.

## What is here

```
main.go       the routes, and the handlers behind them
main_test.go  a test for each route
go.mod        the module
```

`newApp` is separate from `main` so that a test gets the same application the
binary serves. Adding a route means adding a line to `newApp` and a function
under it.
